James inquired about manipulating an arbitrary column in a `dplyr` dataframe using a string to specify the column name. I explained how to achieve this by using the `mutate()` function along with `sym()` and the `:=` operator. I provided an R code snippet demonstrating that the specified column, in this case `mu`, can be modified with the formula `mu * 1e6 / gdp.2015.gbp` by dynamically setting the `column_name` variable. This method allows for flexibility in modifying any column specified as a string within `mutate()`.
